---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactPlate from '../components/ContactPlate.astro';
import EmptyRoom from '../components/floor/EmptyRoom.astro';
import { BACK_TO_STUDIO } from '../lib/copy';

/*
  COPY.md §9 and DESIGN.md §B.11.

  The page is a headline, one link home, and an empty room — the floor slab and the lamp,
  no desks and no chair, drawn from the floor's own defs (see EmptyRoom.astro). COPY.md
  §9 names none of it on purpose: "A line explaining a visual joke kills the joke and
  doubles the page." So the room carries no caption, no alt text and no second link, and
  the whole scene is aria-hidden.

  The room arrives in run C. Run B recorded it as open rather than fixed, because the
  floor's slab and lamp — the two things §B.11 says this page reuses — did not exist as
  shared symbols until then.

  Step-1 review item 13: §B.10's address table lists /404 among the pages that print
  thegeekdogs@gmail.com on the plate, and no plate rendered there at any width. It does
  now, in the same sticky wrapper the home page uses — the wrapper is the page's whole
  content, because /404 has neither a hero to leave nor a final CTA to retire into. The
  plate is site chrome, not this page's link, and COPY.md §9 says so in terms, so it
  stays and the page's own content is still a headline and one link.

  Step-1 review item 15: the page can be shorter than the viewport, so the room section
  grows to fill it and the footer band sits on the viewport's bottom edge. No bare sheet
  shows below the band at any width.

  §J's pre-committed cut for this route, made specific in round 12 and taken here (review
  item E2): `quietFooter` drops the footer's nav repeat and its `Elsewhere` block. §J names
  them by hand — "The empty room is the joke; a nav menu underneath it is not" — and
  rendered, this page was 1,120px of which 615px was footer. The header nav stays, because
  it is site chrome on every route, and so do the studio line, the location line, the
  address, the employer note and the rights line, which are the footer everywhere else.
*/
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Page not found | TheGeekDogs"
  description="That page isn't here. One link back to the studio, and nothing else on it."
  noindex
  quietFooter
>
  <div class="plate-span plate-span--page">
    <section class="section bleed room empty-room section--reserve">
      <div class="shell stack">
        <h1>This page isn't here.</h1>
        <p>
          <a class="link" href="/" aria-label={BACK_TO_STUDIO.accessibleName}>
            {BACK_TO_STUDIO.label}
          </a>
        </p>
        <EmptyRoom />
      </div>
    </section>

    <ContactPlate />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* The wrapper is the page here, so the one section it holds takes the growth and the
     footer band sits on the viewport's bottom edge (step-1 review item 15). */
  .empty-room {
    flex: 1 0 auto;
  }

  /* The room stands away from the line that sent you into it. `.stack` sets the rhythm
     between the headline and the link; this is the one step above it. */
  .empty-room :global(.room404) {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-48);
  }
</style>
